# RCliff₂ derives the decoded Makary–Ross–Selinger relations (Appendices B, F.2, G.2)

The derivations of Appendix B, each replayed line by line from the paper's
figures, and those of Appendix A that the decoding of R13–R16 needs ("one
could straightforwardly mimic the proofs of Equations C12–C15", Appendix
G.2); then the decoding of every relation R1–R16 of Makary, Ross and
Selinger's presentation (`rel_derivable`) and the round trips of the
generators (Appendix F.2, `DE`).  Each step between two printed lines was
found by a search over rewrites modulo commuting gates on disjoint wires,
using the rules the paper cites for that step (and, where the paper applies
a rule in a derived form, its inverse or its image upside down), and is
replayed by `derive`.

Generated by `gen/gen_rcliff.py` from the derivations `gen/run_rcliff.py`
finds (the figures read by `gen/figparse.py`).
-/
import QCert.Minimality.RealClifford.Transfer
